From 1d9744085e622996a675422755cf5f7795003a2c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 02:37:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] windowing/gbm: Dolby Vision for the menus is kept only if the
 user confirms it

Turning the setting on is the same kind of change as a new resolution: a
display that takes the transport badly shows black, and the setting that
did it is in the menus that cannot be seen. Kodi asks "keep this?" with a
countdown after a change of resolution or of monitor and goes back unless
the answer is yes; the setting now does the same (issue 20).

A change from off to on that Kodi sees while it runs is armed
(CDVMenusKeep, tested by itself). Once the menus have really gone out and
the display had 2.5 s to switch its picture mode, the application thread
asks, with a 15 s countdown and "No" as the default button. Only a yes
keeps it; no, Back, the time running out, or a dialog that something else
closed turn the setting off again, which ends the menus by themselves
(CDVMenus::Stays()), and the settings are saved. A question that cannot be
shown for 90 s (another dialog stays open) counts as not kept. Nothing is
asked where nothing changed on the output (the menus could not start), when
the setting was on at the start of Kodi, or when it was turned off again
meanwhile. kodi.log says what was turned on, and whether it was kept or
reverted, and why.
